WEBVTT

00:04.650 --> 00:07.450
This video walks through escape at Clover Bottom.

00:07.450 --> 00:10.263
The maps here are simplified traces of the escapeway

00:10.263 --> 00:13.437
maps for each Clover Bottom mine. The map posted

00:13.437 --> 00:16.188
at the mine always governs. Your instructor will

00:16.188 --> 00:18.800
show you the current maps and walk the escapeways

00:18.800 --> 00:19.562
with you.

00:20.676 --> 00:24.038
Clover Bottom is two separate MSHA mines that share

00:24.038 --> 00:27.239
one surface. The old mine, number one,

00:27.239 --> 00:32.351
has MSHA ID 15-00112. The new mine,

00:32.351 --> 00:39.864
number two, opened in 2021 and has MSHA ID 15-19898.

00:39.864 --> 00:43.063
Both are one-level room-and-pillar limestone mines.

00:43.063 --> 00:45.476
In the old mine, the floor is mined.

00:45.476 --> 00:47.801
In the new mine, headers are mined.

00:48.943 --> 00:51.218
Here's the most important point for this site.

00:51.218 --> 00:54.318
Even though the surface is shared, the escapeways,

00:54.318 --> 00:56.756
the maps, and the procedures are different for

00:56.756 --> 00:59.481
each mine. The way out of the old mine is not the

00:59.481 --> 01:02.281
way out of the new mine. So every shift,

01:02.281 --> 01:05.081
the first question is, which mine am I in today?

01:06.204 --> 01:09.480
Between the two mines is a busy shared surface.

01:09.480 --> 01:12.254
Shot rock is hauled to the pit, where the primary

01:12.254 --> 01:15.105
crusher is, and conveyed up the hill to the secondary

01:15.105 --> 01:18.954
plant. The crew also drills and blasts on the surface.

01:18.954 --> 01:21.529
In an evacuation, you'll come out of a portal into

01:21.529 --> 01:23.817
that traffic, so once you're outside,

01:23.817 --> 01:26.467
stay on the walkways and watch for trucks and loaders

01:26.467 --> 01:29.155
that may not know an emergency is going on.

01:32.482 --> 01:35.232
Every underground mine must keep an accurate record

01:35.232 --> 01:38.032
of who is in the mine, kept on the surface,

01:38.032 --> 01:40.570
and everyone underground must carry a positive

01:40.570 --> 01:43.320
way to be identified. At Clover Bottom,

01:43.320 --> 01:45.945
that means the tag board, and visitors have a separate

01:45.945 --> 01:49.020
check-in. Clover Bottom has one tag board:

01:49.020 --> 01:51.820
in-mine number one on the left, out in the middle,

01:51.820 --> 01:53.745
and in-mine number two on the right.

01:53.745 --> 01:56.169
Tag in under the mine you're actually entering,

01:56.169 --> 01:58.807
every time you go underground, and tag out every

01:58.807 --> 02:00.045
time you come out.

02:01.156 --> 02:03.894
Inspectors have cited check-in and check-out problems

02:03.894 --> 02:07.169
at Clover Bottom three times since 2021.

02:07.169 --> 02:10.219
With two mines on one surface, a tag on the wrong

02:10.219 --> 02:12.806
board means rescuers could search the wrong mine

02:12.806 --> 02:16.181
for you. Never tag in or out for anyone else.

02:19.502 --> 02:22.365
Each mine must have at least two separate escapeways

02:22.365 --> 02:25.502
to the surface, positioned so that damage to one

02:25.502 --> 02:28.190
doesn't block the other. Know the primary and the

02:28.190 --> 02:30.765
secondary from your work area, in the mine you're

02:30.765 --> 02:34.390
in. On the maps, both are marked with green arrows.

02:34.390 --> 02:37.052
A P in the arrow's circle means primary,

02:37.052 --> 02:40.827
and an S means secondary. If someone is hurt underground,

02:40.827 --> 02:43.002
they come out by the primary escapeway.

02:43.002 --> 02:45.640
Any miner can call for help and meet the ambulance

02:45.640 --> 02:46.602
at the portal.

02:47.770 --> 02:50.558
Floor mining and header mining change the openings

02:50.558 --> 02:53.208
as they advance. Routes can change too.

02:53.208 --> 02:55.808
Walk both escapeways with your instructor,

02:55.808 --> 02:58.407
and again whenever your work area moves.

02:59.522 --> 03:01.797
Escape routes are inspected regularly,

03:01.797 --> 03:04.684
kept travelable, and marked with signs that clearly

03:04.684 --> 03:07.760
show the way out. Each mine has a written escape

03:07.760 --> 03:10.922
and evacuation plan, and parts of its map are posted

03:10.922 --> 03:13.984
where people gather. On the maps, escapeways are

03:13.984 --> 03:16.635
marked with green arrows. Underground,

03:16.635 --> 03:19.160
the primary escapeway has white reflectors on the

03:19.160 --> 03:22.222
ribs and the secondary has blue reflectors,

03:22.222 --> 03:25.672
with reflective signs and arrows. Maps are posted

03:25.672 --> 03:28.447
in the breakroom, at the drill steel building near

03:28.447 --> 03:31.172
the Liwell plant for number one, and at the portal

03:31.172 --> 03:33.947
for number two. Product is sometimes stockpiled

03:33.947 --> 03:36.535
underground, so make sure stockpiles and parked

03:36.535 --> 03:38.809
equipment never block an escapeway.

03:38.809 --> 03:40.697
If one does, report it.

03:41.828 --> 03:44.853
If smoke, fire, or a fall of ground blocks your

03:44.853 --> 03:48.591
primary escapeway, turn back and take the secondary.

03:48.591 --> 03:50.691
Stay together with the people around you.

03:50.691 --> 03:53.453
If you get turned around, stop at an intersection

03:53.453 --> 03:56.191
and look for the direction signs before going on.

03:56.191 --> 03:59.716
And remember, in a one-level mine, rooms and crosscuts

03:59.716 --> 04:02.978
can look alike. Knowing landmarks along your route,

04:02.978 --> 04:05.240
like the Liwell plant in the old mine,

04:05.240 --> 04:07.990
a belt line, or a turn at a stockpile,

04:07.990 --> 04:10.203
helps you keep your bearings when visibility is

04:10.203 --> 04:11.016
poor.

04:14.347 --> 04:17.322
The underground fire warning here is stench gas,

04:17.322 --> 04:20.272
released into the intake fan. Warnings also come

04:20.272 --> 04:23.247
by radio and strobe lights. At the first sign of

04:23.247 --> 04:27.772
smoke, a CO alarm, or stench gas, put on your W65

04:27.772 --> 04:30.234
self-rescuer right away, warn others,

04:30.234 --> 04:32.784
and head out by your escapeway. The hot,

04:32.784 --> 04:36.572
dry air from the W65 is normal. Keep it on.

04:37.692 --> 04:40.429
An emergency in one mine can affect the shared

04:40.429 --> 04:42.829
surface too. If you're on the surface,

04:42.829 --> 04:45.217
follow the person in charge, and stay clear of

04:45.217 --> 04:48.167
the portals so people coming out and rescuers have

04:48.167 --> 04:48.779
room.

04:49.890 --> 04:51.940
Once you're out, go to your gathering point on

04:51.940 --> 04:54.890
the surface and report to the person in charge.

04:54.890 --> 04:57.365
Say which mine you came out of, so the count for

04:57.365 --> 04:59.765
each mine is right. Don't go back in unless you're

04:59.765 --> 05:02.653
told to. There's no designated refuge chamber at

05:02.653 --> 05:05.390
Clover Bottom, so the plan is to get out.

05:05.390 --> 05:07.565
Clover Bottom's gathering points are the tag-board

05:07.565 --> 05:10.853
trailer, signed Emergency Assembly Area 1,

05:10.853 --> 05:13.278
the old mine entrance, and behind the mine by the

05:13.278 --> 05:15.440
haul road to the asphalt plant.

05:16.572 --> 05:19.297
You'll practice this. Evacuation drills are held

05:19.297 --> 05:22.060
at least every six months for each shift,

05:22.060 --> 05:24.297
with everyone underground taking part.

05:24.297 --> 05:26.797
They test whether everyone can reach the surface

05:26.797 --> 05:29.335
within the time your self-rescuer gives you.

05:29.335 --> 05:33.235
Treat every drill as real. Take your actual escapeway,

05:33.235 --> 05:35.910
use what you trained on, and notice anything that

05:35.910 --> 05:38.685
slows you down, like a blocked crosscut,

05:38.685 --> 05:41.435
a missing sign, or a door that sticks.

05:41.435 --> 05:42.959
Report it after the drill.

05:44.083 --> 05:46.270
To sum up for Clover Bottom. Know which mine you're

05:46.270 --> 05:48.995
in today. Tag in and out at that mine.

05:48.995 --> 05:52.045
Know that mine's primary and secondary escapeways.

05:52.045 --> 05:55.945
At the first warning, put on your W65 and get out.

05:55.945 --> 05:58.095
And at the gathering point, say which mine you

05:58.095 --> 06:00.858
came from. Fill in your emergency card with your

06:00.858 --> 06:03.670
instructor before your first shift underground.

06:04.800 --> 06:07.963
Remember: your site's plans and procedures always

06:07.963 --> 06:09.463
override this video.
